Architecture plan for Issue #111: Guest / Demo login button

Project shape:
- Rust Axum API in `crates/api`, shared domain/config/repositories in `crates/core`, worker jobs in `crates/worker`.
- React/Vite/Tailwind SPA in `web/`, with routes under `web/src/routes`, feature modules under `web/src/features`, and app shell/provider wiring under `web/src/app`.
- PostgreSQL remains the persistent datastore; seeded demo data is expected to provide `alice@example.test` with password `password123`.

Issue dependency:
- Issue #111 depends on the existing login endpoint and seeded demo user. No backend route should be added.

Implementation approach for #111:
- Update `web/src/routes/LoginPage.tsx` to add a `Guest / Demo Login` button.
- Reuse the existing `auth.login({ email, password })` flow with `alice@example.test` / `password123`.
- Share the existing loading/error behavior so demo login disables controls while submitting and reports failures through the current error message area.
- Preserve the existing redirect behavior after successful login.

Key decisions:
- Keep demo login frontend-only because the issue explicitly forbids a new `/auth/guest` endpoint.
- Do not persist secrets or demo credentials outside the UI behavior requested by the issue.
- Validate with the web build and avoid changes to backend auth semantics.
